{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229400-battle-groups-and-combat-charms-points-of-rupture","id":1229400,"title":"Battle Groups and Combat Charms - Points of Rupture","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-22T10:54:27-07:00","id":1229400,"title":"Battle Groups and Combat Charms - Points of Rupture","content":"I have always thought that there is a correlation between Battle Groups and singular charms. For this I mean that combat charms have effects that work against the bettale groups and separate individuals, work in a more or less linear fashion. You add dice on an attack against a battle group of ten fighters, you add a few dice against ten individual fighters ganging up on you, and that works more or less as it should, but faster an simpler. Doing things faster and simpler is a great ideal, and I'm all for it!<br /> <br /> However, Battle Group and individuals scenarios doen't always map up on a quasi-linear fashion. There are some situations that generate a disconnect. I mostly perceive them when I'm describing the effects to new players, who haven't digested and interiorized the system. For instance, we have Ovwewhelming Panaltis negators. They are completely necessary when fighting against ten individuals. There is basically no way even an amateur attacker won't have a free pass at you, if you get attacked by ten of them, On the other hand, the benefit of a penalty negator against a battle group of ten is... none?<br /> <br /> I use a lot of battle groups, since its neater and faster. So I see that there are some charms that basically never used. All enemies of the same type do a battlegroup, and then there are a few heroes. That's it. The players pick their targets, and there is no real place for someone taking serious overwhelming penalties.<br /> <br /> Let me give you one example: I had a new player wanting to use Dipping Swallow defense against a battle group. I could have told her 'that does nothing'. But, I've decided to negate the size bonus on the attack roll. Now, that's better than nothing, but it created other complications, such as what would happen when one player uses a penalty negator and other don't. I haven't had problem with penalty negators after this, because my players don't use penalty negators. It's DV increase with excellencies and all attack, all the time, why bother with a -1, at most? This is a big problem, because One True Strategies are somewhat boring. So I've being thinking of ways to get these 'useless' charms some use.<br /> <br /> What other problems do you see in fights against Battle Groups, and what type of house rules you've implemented?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T13:18:43-07:00","id":1229437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229400-battle-groups-and-combat-charms-points-of-rupture#post1229400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me give you one example: I had a new player wanting to use Dipping Swallow defense against a battle group. I could have told her 'that does nothing'. But, I've decided to negate the size bonus on the attack roll. Now, that's better than nothing, but it created other complications, such as what would happen when one player uses a penalty negator and other don't.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...How is this a complication?<br /> <br /> You roll the size-less attack pool, apply successes against the first player, then you roll (size) extra dice, add the result to the original attack successes and apply the result against the rest.<br /> <br /> It doesn't even meaningfully slow down play, because there's no way you'd roll all the dice at the same time (unless you truly have an absurd number of them on hand)!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T14:51:22-07:00","id":1229460,"title":"","content":"I tend to roll all the dice at once, because I use a dice roller.<br /> <br /> Although what I do, if rolling extra dice vs one person, is I'll roll, say, 15 dice, and ignore the last 3 dice if there's only 12 dice against the other person.<br /> <br /> <br /> TBH though, I haven't bothered with any House Rules with battle groups, and it hasn't really been a problem.<br /> I don't really mind if PCs don't take a ton of Overwhelming. That just means the players are less likely to make mistakes when calculating their Defence.<br /> <br /> The battle groups I used were generally either chumps whose job was to die in a few turns and make the PCs look cool, or Tiger Warriors who were actually quite threatening. Not much in the middle. Not sure if that makes a difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T15:07:57-07:00","id":1229462,"title":"","content":"While Dipping Swallow Defense specifically is totally forgivable, the fact that there\u2019s so many charms meant for fighting multiple people that don\u2019t do anything against the most common kind of \u201cmultiple people\u201d is definitely something that\u2019s bugged me for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T17:24:01-07:00","id":1229487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229400-battle-groups-and-combat-charms-points-of-rupture?p=1229437#post1229437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ...How is this a complication?<br /> <br /> You roll the size-less attack pool, apply successes against the first player, then you roll (size) extra dice, add the result to the original attack successes and apply the result against the rest.<br /> <br /> It doesn't even meaningfully slow down play, because there's no way you'd roll all the dice at the same time (unless you truly have an absurd number of them on hand)!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I do roll all of them at once, in a wood box. Separating the dice would be a mess! Even more so with more battle groups.<br /> <br /> Perhaps just subtracting Size/2 successes would be more a faster, more elegant solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T23:50:50-07:00","id":1229534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229400-battle-groups-and-combat-charms-points-of-rupture?p=1229462#post1229462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Dipping Swallow Defense specifically is totally forgivable, the fact that there\u2019s so many charms meant for fighting multiple people that don\u2019t do anything against the most common kind of \u201cmultiple people\u201d is definitely something that\u2019s bugged me for a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true. It hasn't come up for us because I think the PCs just don't have those charms*, but I do agree that charms that do things like attack everyone in short range should have some bonus against battle groups.<br /> <br /> *Thinking about it, one has the charm where you grapple someone and throw them into someone else, creating a shockwave that hits others. But they've never used it against a battle group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T02:41:07-07:00","id":1229553,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this is definitely an oversight.<br /> <br /> Someone should go over the multiple opponents charms and give them all alternate effects that make sense against a battle group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T07:03:33-07:00","id":1229587,"title":"","content":"I think if charms that deal with Overwhelming penalties also negate Size you've just created a different one true-strategy to dealing with Battle Groups, namely throw up Fivefold Bulwark and laugh at the stupid mortals trying to hurt you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T19:37:24-07:00","id":1235777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229400-battle-groups-and-combat-charms-points-of-rupture?p=1229587#post1229587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if charms that deal with Overwhelming penalties also negate Size you've just created a different one true-strategy to dealing with Battle Groups, namely throw up Fivefold Bulwark and laugh at the stupid mortals trying to hurt you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, battle groups will still have might bonuses, control bonuses and size will still count for damage, soak and magnitude. It's hardly a complete negation.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Fivefold Bulwark Stance needs a little love, being simple and all. I do use combat groups a lot to speed things up, so it's rare that a character will face lots of individual opponents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T21:01:07-07:00","id":1235796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229400-battle-groups-and-combat-charms-points-of-rupture?p=1235777#post1235777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do use combat groups a lot to speed things up...</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's not what battle groups are <i>for</i>. Battle groups aren't meant to serve as an abstraction of many individuals for quicker combat resolution; it's there to emulate the genre trait of heroes cutting through tens, scores, or even legions of relatively-faceless enemies. If we were recreating, for instance, Conan facing off against the Rebel Four and their would-be kingslayers, I'd use individual stats for Volmana, Gromel, Rinaldo, and Ascalante, but the other sixteen men would just be a battle group.<br /> <br /> \u200b(And of course, halfway through, an Erythmanus jumps in, on a mission of its own...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-17-2018, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T00:57:13-07:00","id":1235829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229400-battle-groups-and-combat-charms-points-of-rupture?p=1235796#post1235796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's not what battle groups are <i>for</i>. Battle groups aren't meant to serve as an abstraction of many individuals for quicker combat resolution; it's there to emulate the genre trait of heroes cutting through tens, scores, or even legions of relatively-faceless enemies. <br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not both?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T03:44:55-07:00","id":1235855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229400-battle-groups-and-combat-charms-points-of-rupture?p=1235829#post1235829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not both?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because while Battle Groups are fast it's faster still to dispense with join battle entirely and have everyone just stunt and roll (Dexterity + Combat Ability).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T09:22:47-07:00","id":1235962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229400-battle-groups-and-combat-charms-points-of-rupture?p=1235855#post1235855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because while Battle Groups are fast it's faster still to dispense with join battle entirely and have everyone just stunt and roll (Dexterity + Combat Ability).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a little too reductivist for my taste. The way I do, I can have both use of the charms that the players purchased, and also have a combat that doesn't take forever. And let's not forget, in my way the combat characters can also have a challenge, healers got things to heal, and so on, in a happy ecosystem.<br /> <br /> If things by any chance get so undemanding to the point where the characters could just make one roll and decide, I simply let them narrate what they want to do, instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T10:15:34-07:00","id":1235985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229400-battle-groups-and-combat-charms-points-of-rupture?p=1235855#post1235855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because while Battle Groups are fast it's faster still to dispense with join battle entirely and have everyone just stunt and roll (Dexterity + Combat Ability).</div> </div> </div> </div>I do that occasionally, when the fight is pretty minor. Like, bopping a guard over the back of the head.<br /> <br /> But I think it's reasonable to want to have an interesting fight that doesn't take over 2 hours, yet also takes more than 2 rounds. There's a good balance to be had, and battle groups do a good job with that.<br /> <br /> That's why I like to use 1-2 NPCs plus a battle group for fights; this gives you a fun fight with a couple of significant characters that is a bit of a challenge for the PCs (but not really difficult), doesn't feel like the antagonists would realise they're utterly outmatched (because they're outnumbered) but it generally takes an hour to an hour and a half. I think that's a good amount of time for a fight.<br /> For example, a couple of enemy Solars plus 20 Tiger Warriors, or a sorcerer and his 7-10 elemental bodyguards, or a 2nd circle demon and a pack of bisclaravets.<br /> Or a Zenith with 1000 Tiger Warriors. That was a good fight.<br /> <br /> If you just have 1-2 NPCs, I find the PCs put them down really quickly, and you often wonder why the NPCs didn't bring any guards.<br /> If you have 5-6 NPCs, on the other hand, it takes ages (and it's quite difficult to keep track of all their charms and different stats; battle groups are much easier to run).<br /> <br /> So, during my campaign, I mostly used NPCs+battle groups for fights, and I only used more than 1-2 NPCs with charms twice; once for a Wyld Hunt, and once for the final battle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-17-2018, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T12:45:43-07:00","id":1236075,"title":"","content":"What you could do is have a battle group that one or two individual fighters precipitate out of occasionally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T13:02:43-07:00","id":1236085,"title":"","content":"Okay I think there's been a minor misunderstanding. From the response to Alucard's post I was under the impression we were talking about named individuals being rolled into a Battle Group for the sake of expedience. I'm behind named character + bodyguards as an encounter.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't find that battle groups save me much time. I've noticed consistently that the action my players spend the most time procrastinating on is their defence, which makes sense. Most of them are planning their combat actions during someone else's turn but when it comes to defending themselves they're reacting to me so stunting/checking charms etc in real time and things drag as a result, thus a battle group's area attack takes as long to resolve as the slowest person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 07-17-2018, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T15:27:17-07:00","id":1236172,"title":"","content":"Ah, interesting. My players are the opposite; they generally know their defence charms better than their attack charms (I think because they tend to be used in combination less, and they have more similar names/concepts to their 2nd ed versions) so they tend to respond to attacks much quicker than they actually make attacks.<br /> (Social influence is different, half of them can't even remember what their Resolve is)<br /> <br /> Also, generally speaking, Battle Groups don't actually attack all of the PCs; some charge in and fight up close, but others stay at range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-17-2018, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T03:15:57-07:00","id":1236347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229400-battle-groups-and-combat-charms-points-of-rupture?p=1236172#post1236172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, interesting. My players are the opposite; they generally know their defence charms better than their attack charms (I think because they tend to be used in combination less, and they have more similar names/concepts to their 2nd ed versions) so they tend to respond to attacks much quicker than they actually make attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>This could be partially down to medium. Most of the games I'm talking about are online, if you play face to face it's kinda rude to spend other people's turns browsing through the rulebook and searching the internet.<br /> <br /> But yes it's often not a matter of people knowing their charms so much as the Battle Groups being able to target the people who aren't in a fantastic position combat wise and could easily die if the dice roll doesn't go in their favour.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T06:46:02-07:00","id":1237479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229400-battle-groups-and-combat-charms-points-of-rupture?p=1236347#post1236347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This could be partially down to medium. Most of the games I'm talking about are online, if you play face to face it's kinda rude to spend other people's turns browsing through the rulebook and searching the internet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just be glad that they're doing something game-related. In my experience, the moment they're not being asked to do something, it's back to rattling off memes and yammering about which piece of pop culture this vaguely resembles.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}